d46","inline:4253217673":"dd595231dee3c124ca6176c4d9bb2ac2c6b7cd46","review:5497023472":"dd595231dee3c124ca6176c4d9bb2ac2c6b7cd46"},"parent":"7108e7818b085183e0b27dba9b6ddd2d453902eb","patch_sha256":"2eeca31282de6f0306b2304c40cf8fb3cef4ae5ae157c84d3cdc4fa0905ac39c","tree":"475a59f587ea100432df5f028f6dd1283cdd0fd8"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"The overview summarizes the five warranted inline findings. Commit 1 excludes the Couchbase constructor compatibility suites, both Jedis 2.3 compatibility tasks, and all three filtered receive-span suppression tasks from metadata collection. The repository telemetry-collection policy independently requires these exclusions. Actual Gradle configuration assertions verified collection settings and check membership for all 24 affected and representative tasks.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5497023472"},{"analysis":"CouchbaseProtostellar343Test.capturesTargetWithLegacyConstructors and CouchbaseProtostellar344Test.capturesTargetWithOriginalConstructor each cover one constructor compatibility regression. instrumentation-docs/readme.md:37-44 excludes classpath compatibility regressions. Both version343Test and version344Test now receive collectMetadata=false even with -PcollectMetadata=true, remain enabled in check, and leave the representative Couchbase test variants collection-enabled.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4253217519"},{"analysis":"Jedis23ClusterCommandTest.zeroArgumentExecuteIsInstrumented is a single API compatibility regression. Both version23Test and its version23TestPreviewSemconv variant now receive collectMetadata=false. The excluded preview variant no longer has metadataConfig, as required by the collection policy; it retains the service.peer preview setting and remains in check. The representative testPreviewSemconv still collects and retains its metadataConfig label.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4253217563"},{"analysis":"The JMS 1.1 build filters testReceiveSpansDisabled to Jms1SuppressReceiveSpansTest, whose only parameterized operation verifies suppression behavior. This is not a full representative default-profile suite. The task now receives collectMetadata=false and remains enabled in check, while test and jms2Test retain their collection settings and distinct profile labels.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4253217598"},{"analysis":"The JMS 3.0 build filters testReceiveSpansDisabled to Jms3SuppressReceiveSpansTest, a receive-span suppression regression. It now receives collectMetadata=false while remaining enabled in check. The representative test task continues to collect with its existing receive-telemetry profile.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4253217632"},{"analysis":"Spring JMS 6.0 filters testReceiveSpansDisabled to SpringListenerSuppressReceiveSpansTest, which asserts the receive-span suppression scenario rather than the complete integration suite. It now receives collectMetadata=false and remains enabled in check. The representative test and separately labeled testJmsDisabled mode keep their collection settings.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4253217673"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"bedd899b35e30cb6b31269f985d92dbf659561a75c9049ce87fc48a425519058","schema":2},"download_sha256":"5b8eb0fd3a744f4ef6ede46759213bc3e7b25a47336fe19887b032bb1b65d8c8","frozen_sha":"7108e7818b085183e0b27dba9b6ddd2d453902eb","pr":20549,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"bedd899b35e30cb6b31269f985d92dbf659561a75c9049ce87fc48a425519058","request_id":"952af8eefe724a0693ad9ad78ff57e44","run_attempt":1,"run_id":38324156015,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:5b8eb0fd3a744f4ef6ede46759213bc3e7b25a47336fe19887b032bb1b65d8c8","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":3832677